# Production build configuration for `npm run build`.
#
# This file is COMMITTED on purpose. It holds no secret: the Worker URL is a
# public endpoint that ships inside the JS bundle either way. What it buys is
# that the backend is an explicit, reviewable deployment choice instead of the
# hardcoded BUILTIN_PRODUCTION_WORKER fallback in src/services/cloudConfig.ts —
# which is what produced this warning on every production page load:
#
#   [cloudConfig] VITE_CLOUDFLARE_WORKER_URL was not set at build time; falling
#   back to the built-in Worker https://api.engaz.tech
#
# HANDING THIS PROJECT TO A NEW OPERATOR: point this at the new Worker before
# the first build, and update `routes` + `ALLOWED_ORIGINS` in
# cloudflare-worker/wrangler.toml to match. Secrets never belong in this file —
# see cloudflare-worker/wrangler.toml for the `wrangler secret put` list.
VITE_CLOUDFLARE_WORKER_URL=https://api.engaz.tech
